tisan polls since July, and Dembo's slight cash and outside-spending edge keep the expected margin modest.", "watch": "Independent polling in the final weeks confirming or refuting the Democratic internals, or a shift in the national environment, could push this into genuine tossup territory.", "confidence": "medium", "notes": ["Open seat: Andy Barr (R) is not on the ballot."]}, "overview": "Kentucky's 6th District is an open seat after Andy Barr left to run for Senate, and Republican Ralph Alvarado faces Democrat Zach Dembo in a district that leans Republican by about seven points. Most professional raters call the race Lean Republican, though several moved ratings toward Democrats in late September. Prediction markets give Democrats roughly a one-in-four chance.\n\nThe contest is closer than the district's lean suggests. Democratic-sponsored polls since July show a dead heat, with the most recent giving Dembo a one-point edge, though partisan sponsors warrant caution. Fundraising is nearly even, with Dembo holding slightly more cash and drawing more outside spending. Governor Andy Beshear's push to flip the seat and a Trump-versus-Beshear ad war signal that both parties see real opportunity here, keeping the race competitive but tilting Republican.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.2515, "margin": -3.92}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.296, "margin": -4.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.2877, "margin": -4.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.2982, "margin": -4.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.223, "margin": -4.5}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.2389, "margin": -4.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.2735, "margin": -4.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.2956, "margin": -4.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.2849, "margin": -4.0}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.3514, "margin": -3.0}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.3215, "margin": -3.5}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.3486, "margin": -3.0}]}